        "title": "Devotion and Grace Personified by Lord Siva",
        "text": "This temple is a must see place, when visiting Kathmandu. You can get a complete feel of Hindu culture and Vedic traditions at the site; filled with incense sticks, mantras in the air and bells ring.\nThis temple has 4 doors and the deity can be seen from all the four doors and stays always crowded. Photography and wearing shoes/slippers are not allowed in the temple premises. There are a lot of stores selling Rudraksha beads around the temple and do check for the authenticity before you buy them with a good bargain.\nYou can feed pigeons or give any offerings to the temple as wished. Kindly avoid the river banks at the end of the temple as that location is used for cremating the dead (As per Hindu Traditions).",
